{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JHN",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the third day there was a marriage in Cana of Galilee; and the mother of Jesus was there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And both Jesus was called, and his disciples, to the marriage.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they wanted wine, the mother of Jesus saith to him, They have no wine.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to her, Woman, what have I to do with thee? my hour is not yet come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His mother saith to the servants, Whatever he saith to you, do ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And there were set there six waterpots of stone, after the manner of the purifying of the Jews, containing two or three firkins apiece.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to them, Fill the waterpots with water. And they filled them to the brim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he saith to them, Draw out now, and bear to the governor of the feast. And they bore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When the ruler of the feast had tasted the water that was made wine, and knew not whence it was; (but the servants who drew the water knew) the governor of the feast called the bridegroom,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And saith to him, Every man at the beginning presenteth good wine; and when men have well drank, then that which is worse: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast kept the good wine until now.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This beginning of miracles Jesus performed in Cana of Galilee, and manifested his glory; and his disciples believed on him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "After this he went down to Capernaum, he, and his mother, and his brethren, and his disciples; and they continued there not many days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the Jews' passover was at hand, and Jesus went up to Jerusalem,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And found in the temple those that sold oxen, and sheep, and doves, and the changers of money, sitting:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had made a scourge of small cords, he drove them all out of the temple, and the sheep, and the oxen; and poured out the changers' money, and overthrew the tables;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to them that sold doves, Take these things hence: make not my Father's house a house of merchandise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his disciples remembered that it was written, The zeal of thy house hath eaten me up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered the Jews, and said to him, What sign showest thou to us, seeing that thou doest these things?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered and said to them, Destroy this temple, and in three days I will raise it up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said the Jews, Forty and six years was this temple in building, and wilt thou rear it up in three days?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he spoke of the temple of his body.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When therefore he had risen from the dead, his disciples remembered that he had said this to them: and they believed the scripture, and the word which Jesus had spoken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now when he was in Jerusalem at the passover, in the feast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "day",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", many believed in his name, when they saw the miracles which he performed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus did not commit himself to them, because he knew all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.2.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.2.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And needed not that any should testify concerning man: for he knew what was in man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
